  "read": "On 500 films from 132 patients the watermark contagion is +0.708; resampling patients gives [0.5944, 0.8003], against [0.668, 0.748] resampling films. Inside the 500, the 35-film cohort's isolated reads differ from this lineage's committed n=35 run on 0 of 35 films (0 now adopting, 0 now holding) and its shared reads agree on 35; on the 150 films of this lineage's earlier 150-film run, contagion was 0.66 then and is 0.6533 now. Shared adoption is at the ceiling (0.994, 497 of 500 films), so this difference is 1 minus isolated adoption (0.286, resampling patients [0.1951, 0.3985]) to within 0.006; shared adoption is also at the ceiling on nih_80 and chexpert_150. Compare cohorts and lineages on isolated adoption (watermark_cascade_by_cohort), not on the difference."
